# The PostgreSQL archive each release installer carries, one per target
# `release.yml` builds: `<sha256>  <asset>` of
# https://github.com/theseus-rs/postgresql-binaries/releases/tag/<version>.
# `scripts/fetch-postgres.sh` downloads the one for its target and refuses a
# file that does not match. Each target's version is `knobas-db`'s
# `PG_VERSION_REQ` on that platform (`crates/knobas-app/src/postgres.rs` has
# the test), so the two move together. Linux is on theseus's 18.6.1, which
# carries its libraries (docs/decisions/2026-11-23-linux-postgresql-carries-its-libraries.md).
a257bcdb8aa3301a13d6a5bcec48f8c9517045b7cbae71e50788b2615539e95b  postgresql-18.6.0-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz
7da44c2dbcda3b49688ea08ce8cf99cfe677adf565f53a9145bf9002c74db7d5  postgresql-18.6.0-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.tar.gz
e84b02dd8d0ce5879fb697330a789231c8b8f8d958dae3ad4d90fecc710b1315  postgresql-18.6.1-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz
